# Blossoming Tortoise: "Activated abilities of lands you control cost {1} less" and "land creatures you control get +1/+1" are about
# your lands only. Bot1's three milled cards on turn 1 are Ornithopters, so no land is returned (a land card is needed). On turn 2
# Bot2's own Mutavault is not reduced: its {1} is paid in full by tapping the Mutavault itself for {C} (nothing is left in the pool), and it is a plain 2/2. On turn 3
# Bot1's Gingerbrute, an artifact creature not a land, pays its full {1} from the Island (nothing is left in the pool) and is not pumped (1/1); and with
# one Island left a Blasted Landscape in hand still cannot be cycled for {2}, an ability a land has outside the battlefield not being reduced.

